This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

This is a live, timed (24h clock) Vela Developer Practical Challenge: build a real, working, headless conversational booking agent for padel/tennis + hotel trips against the real House of Journeys (HOFJ) API, with real Stripe test-mode payment, deployed live on Cloudflare Workers. The original brief (pasted as the first message) specified non-negotiable constraints: no results pages/lists/comparison grids ever; one proposal at a time, never two options in the same message (only offer an alternative after explicit rejection); the entire purchase starts from one natural-language intent; the interface must be voice-first (attention off-screen is the actual reason, not just "chat instead of a list"); real accessibility (not all buyers have eyes/a screen/patience); Vela is not a destination (the agent comes to the traveller); scope is padel/tennis + hotel only. Pattern: slot-filling → negotiation on mismatches → single proposal with price → explicit confirmation → silent re-verification of price/availability → real booking + payment → operational summary. Stack fixed as TypeScript/Cloudflare Workers/Durable Objects/wrangler/npm/vitest. Confidence must be categorical (exact/compromise/none), never a fake numeric score. Deliverables: live URL, public repo with real history, ARCHITECTURE.md updated live, /agent-log/ raw transcripts, k6 load test with real numbers, 3-5 min demo video. Evaluators cross-reference agent-log timestamps, commit history, and pause/resume events — a messy repo with a clear, well-directed agent trail scores well; a tidy repo with no evidence of process scores badly.

Over the course of the session, the user (Giuseppe) progressively steered toward: (a) fixing every real bug found through live testing, verified empirically rather than assumed; (b) an explicit precision policy — budget and party size (adults) must never be silently decided, always asked; location/date/teacher-preference may be decided by the agent when vague, but always disclosed as an explicit "compromise" requiring confirmation, never a hidden choice; (c) most recently, closing the gap toward a specific target customer-journey example (English, multi-slot single utterance, qualitative budget/location, month-only date, near-invisible traveller-data collection, "confirmed" price before asking to book) by implementing: language mirroring, a location "shortlist" reasoning eventually (not yet fully built), a mid-tier budget qualifier, month-awareness in date resolution, a demo user profile (stand-in for future real per-user login/profiles), and wiring a direct Stripe PaymentIntent creation as a sanctioned bypass for HOFJ's broken payment endpoint, using Carlo's (Vela contact) latest guidance about `paymentType` ("full" vs "plan").

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- Cloudflare Workers + Durable Objects (one DO per conversation, naturally serializing turns — also the double-booking guard)
- Workers AI (Llama 3.3 70B, `@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast`) as primary NLU/NLG engine, Anthropic Haiku (`claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`) as fallback (activated after Workers AI's daily free-tier neuron quota was exhausted mid-session, error 4006)
- Deterministic vs LLM-owned logic split: all calendar math, city/product matching, and price/compromise classification live in code (testable, auditable); the LLM only does NLU (slot extraction) and NLG (phrasing) — repeatedly reinforced principle after finding the LLM cannot reliably do date arithmetic
- Categorical confidence pattern: `ConfidenceCategory = "exact" | "compromise" | "none"`, with typed `compromise.kind` variants: `"price" | "date" | "date_unspecified" | "location_unspecified" | "budget_unspecified"`
- "Gating-satisfied" slot-filling loop-breaker pattern (per-slot attempt counters: `cityAskAttempts`, `budgetAskAttempts`, with `CITY_LOOP_BREAKER = 2`, `BUDGET_LOOP_BREAKER = 1`), with `adults` deliberately exempt (never bypassed)
- HOFJ Distribution API: Terrarossa (terrarossa.com) is the tennis/padel brand of record, Weebora (weebora.com) is a fallback with its own padel inventory; House of Journey (booking.hofj.com) is unrelated
