New exported function:
```typescript
export function extractMonthHint(raw: string | null): number | null {
  if (!raw) return null;
  const text = raw.trim().toLowerCase();
  const match = text.match(new RegExp(`\\b(${MONTH_NAMES_PATTERN})\\b`));
  if (!match) return null;
  return MONTHS[match[1]!.toLowerCase()]!;
}
```
Purpose: extract a bare month reference from a vague date phrase ("in June") that doesn't resolve to an exact day, to bias candidate selection/date offering toward that month instead of ignoring it entirely (the "December instead of June" regression).

### `src/engine/matcher.ts`
Core deterministic matching logic. Most recent changes:
- Added `pad2()` and `firstDateInMonth(minDate, maxDate, month)` helper — finds the first date within a candidate's availability range that falls in a given month, checking every year the range spans:
```typescript
function firstDateInMonth(minDate: string, maxDate: string, month: number): string | null {
  const start = new Date(`${minDate}T00:00:00Z`);
  const end = new Date(`${maxDate}T00:00:00Z`);
  for (let year = start.getUTCFullYear(); year <= end.getUTCFullYear(); year++) {
    const monthStart = new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, 1));
    const monthEnd = new Date(Date.UTC(year, month, 0));
    const overlapStart = monthStart > start ? monthStart : start;
    const overlapEnd = monthEnd < end ? monthEnd : end;
    if (overlapStart <= overlapEnd) {
      return `${overlapStart.getUTCFullYear()}-${pad2(overlapStart.getUTCMonth() + 1)}-${pad2(overlapStart.getUTCDate())}`;
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```
